  "answer": "I'll start by reading the project skill and locating how the storefront cart API and store merchant settings work.The cart limit belongs in the storefront facade, checked before any save, and read from merchant configuration on each request.The storefront cart API now rejects any create, add, or quantity change that would put more than N units on one cart line, returning HTTP 400 and leaving the cart unchanged. N is read on each request from the store merchant configuration key `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY`, and is 99 when that setting is absent. A quantity of 0 still removes the line. The check lives in `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl` and covers `POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi`.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 responses and that the cart is unchanged when a line exceeds N\", \"that a configuration change applies without a restart\"], \"missing\": [\"an integration test or fixture that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and calls the cart endpoints\"]}",
